Used by: The section that services the committee.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraphs 7.2(viii), 7.14.
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the urgency grading, at the very top
2. the file number
3. the letterhead — Ministry, Department and office
4. the place and date
5. the form’s own title, centred
6. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
7. the body paragraphs
8. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
9. the addressee block
10. the list of enclosures
11. the copy-to list

Rules:
- Write in the THIRD person throughout — "the undersigned", "it is requested", never "I" or "we".
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- An urgency grading (Immediate / Priority / Top Priority — तत्काल / प्राथमिकता / परम अग्रता) may be shown at the top. Grade it only if the officer asked for one; an ungraded communication is the normal case.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Number and date are on the draft — Every draft put up on a file bears the file number, and the number and date of the last communication in the series must be quoted.
- Signature block carries designation, telephone and email — The name, designation, telephone number, fax number and e-mail address of the signing officer must invariably be on the draft.
- The decision sought is stated — A note that describes a problem without saying what is being asked for leaves the committee to draft the proposal itself.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- urgency: none
- fileNumber: A-11011/2/2026-Estt.
- ministry: Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions
- department: Department of Personnel and Training
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- addressee: The Under Secretary
Department of Expenditure
North Block, New Delhi
- subject: Agenda item 3 — revision of the Recruitment Rules for the post of Assistant Section Officer.
- paras: The item is placed before the Departmental Promotion Committee at its meeting to be held on 20.09.2026.
# Background
The Recruitment Rules for the post were last notified in 2011 and do not reflect the restructuring of the Section carried out in 2024.
# The issue
Whether the qualifying service for promotion should be reduced from eight years to five.
# What the rules provide
The Department of Personnel and Training's model Recruitment Rules provide for five years' qualifying service at this level.
# Decision sought
The Committee may approve the reduction of the qualifying service to five years and the issue of the revised Rules.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Under Secretary to the Govt. of India
- phone: 011-2309 2590
- email: us-estt@nic.in
- enclosures: The draft Recruitment Rules, 2026.
- copyTo: All members of the Committee.
The agenda file.

Still empty: committee, meetingDate, background, issue, provision, decisionSought."
`;

exports[`every form has an instruction > appeal 1`] = `
"Form: Appeal to the appellate authority / अपीलीय प्राधिकारी को अपील (id: appeal).
Used by: An officer, on their own behalf.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraph 8.4(1).
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the place and date
2. the addressee block
3. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
4. the salutation
5. the body paragraphs
6. the subscription
7. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
8. the list of enclosures

Rules:
- Write in the FIRST person — this form is one named officer writing to another.
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- This form carries NO urgency grading.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- The date of the order and of its delivery are given — Rule 25 runs the forty-five days from the date the order was delivered. An appeal that gives neither date invites a preliminary objection instead of an answer.
- The language is courteous and temperate — Rule 24 requires an appeal to be couched in courteous and temperate language and free from any disrespectful or improper expression.
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Paragraphs are serially numbered — The specimens leave the first paragraph unnumbered and number the rest from 2.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- addressee: The Joint Secretary (Administration)
Department of Personnel and Training
North Block, New Delhi
(through the Under Secretary (Establishment))
- subject: Appeal under rule 23 of the CCS (CCA) Rules, 1965 against the order dated 12.08.2026.
- paras: This appeal is preferred under rule 23 of the Central Civil Services (Classification, Control and Appeal) Rules, 1965 against the order No. A-11012/7/2026-Vig. dated 12.08.2026, by which the penalty of censure was imposed upon me under rule 11(i) of the said Rules. The order was delivered to me on 18.08.2026 and this appeal is within the forty-five days allowed by rule 25.
# Grounds of appeal
# Prayer
It is prayed that the impugned order may be set aside and the penalty quashed.
The appeal is complete in itself and does not contain any disrespectful or improper language.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Section Officer
- phone: 011-2309 2590
- email: abc@nic.in
- enclosures: A copy of the order dated 12.08.2026 appealed against.

Still empty: orderNumber, orderDate, deliveryDate, whatWasOrdered, grounds, prayer."
`;

