exports[`every form has an instruction > demi-official 1`] = `
"Form: Demi-official letter (D.O.) / अर्ध-सरकारी पत्र (डी.ओ.) (id: demi-official).
Used by: One Government officer writing to another to draw their personal attention to an official matter of importance or urgency; also to a non-official, and by a Minister to another Minister or a Member of Parliament.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraphs 8.4(2), 9.5, Appendix 8.1.

Structure:
1. the letterhead — Ministry, Department and office
2. the file number
3. the place and date
4. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
5. the salutation
6. the body paragraphs
7. the subscription
8. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
9. the addressee block
10. the list of enclosures

Rules:
- Write in the FIRST person — this form is one named officer writing to another.
- Open with the salutation "My dear Shri / Dear Shri".
- Close with the subscription "Yours sincerely,".
- This form carries NO urgency grading.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.
- A D.O. is written from one named officer to another, in the FIRST person, signed with the writer’s own name and no designation above it (CSMOP 8.4(2)).

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- Written in the first person — The object of a D.O. is to invite the addressee's personal attention, so the style is direct, personal and friendly.
- Signed by name, with the sender's designation at the head — A D.O. carries the writer's name and designation at the top left and is signed by name — it is a personal communication.
- Enclosures mentioned in the text are listed — A draft should clearly specify the enclosures which are to accompany the fair copy, and the number goes at the bottom left.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- fileNumber: A-11011/2/2026-Estt.
- ministry: Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions
- department: Department of Personnel and Training
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- addresseeName: Shri R. K. Sharma
- addressee: Shri R. K. Sharma
Joint Secretary
Ministry of Finance
Department of Expenditure
North Block, New Delhi - 110001
- paras: We propose to draw up a model scheme for the training of newly recruited Assistant Section Officers; a copy of the outline prepared in this connection is enclosed.
I shall be grateful if you would let me have your comments as soon as possible. I may add that we intend circulating the draft scheme formally to all Departments in due course for their comments.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Deputy Secretary to the Govt. of India
- phone: 011-2309 2590
- email: us-estt@nic.in
