"Form: Inter-Departmental note (U.O. note) / अंतर-विभागीय टिप्पणी (यू.ओ. टिप्पणी) (id: id-note).
Used by: One Ministry or Department consulting another — for advice, views, comments or concurrence on a proposal, or for a clarification of existing rules from the nodal Department. Also between a Department and its attached and subordinate offices.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraphs 8.1, 8.1.2(v), 8.1.2(vi), 9.6(iv), Appendix 8.1.

Structure:
1. the urgency grading, at the very top
2. the letterhead — Ministry, Department and office
3. the form’s own title, centred
4. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
5. the body paragraphs
6. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
7. the addressee block
8. the list of enclosures
9. the footer

Rules:
- Write in the THIRD person throughout — "the undersigned", "it is requested", never "I" or "we".
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- An urgency grading (Immediate / Priority / Top Priority — तत्काल / प्राथमिकता / परम अग्रता) may be shown at the top. Grade it only if the officer asked for one; an ungraded communication is the normal case.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.
- An inter-departmental note asks another Department for its views and is returned on the same file; it never conveys a decision (CSMOP 8.4(6)).

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- Every paragraph is numbered, from 1 — The Appendix 8.1 specimen of an I.D. note numbers its first paragraph 1, unlike a letter or an O.M.
- The point on which advice is sought is in the last paragraph — Clearly state the points on which the advice or concurrence of the other Department is sought, preferably in the concluding paragraph.
- A time limit is prescribed — Prescribe a time limit when calling for advice or concurrence; without one the originating Ministry has nothing to wait until.
- I.D. number and date are at the foot — The specimen closes with 'Department of … I.D. No. … dated …' below a rule.
- Signed at Under Secretary level or above — Inter-Departmental references are made with the approval of an officer not below Joint Secretary, under the signature of an officer not below Under Secretary.
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Enclosures mentioned in the text are listed — A draft should clearly specify the enclosures which are to accompany the fair copy, and the number goes at the bottom left.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- urgency: none
- ministry: Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions
- department: Department of Personnel and Training
- subject: Grant of Children Education Allowance — clarification regarding.
- paras: The present rules regulating the issue of identity cards provide, inter alia, that a card is to be surrendered on the date of superannuation.
A question has now arisen whether an officer re-employed immediately on superannuation may retain the card issued to him before retirement.
The matter has been examined in this Department. The rules are silent on re-employment, and no precedent is available on the file.
It is felt that a card carrying the pre-retirement designation would be misleading and that a fresh card should be issued.
This Department will be grateful for the advice of the Department of Legal Affairs on the issue raised in para 4 above. Comments are requested by 30.09.2026, please.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Deputy Secretary
- phone: 011-2309 2590
- email: us-estt@nic.in
- addressee: Department of Legal Affairs (Vidhi Karya Vibhag), Shri A. K. Menon, Shastri Bhawan, New Delhi
- idNumber: A-11011/2/2026-Estt.
- date: 2026-08-28
- enclosures: Draft instructions proposed to be issued (1 page)

Still empty: mainPoint."
`;

exports[`every form has an instruction > interim-reply 1`] = `
"Form: Interim reply / अंतरिम उत्तर (id: interim-reply).
Used by: Any section that cannot reply finally within the time limit.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraphs 8.9(ii), 8.10.
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the urgency grading, at the very top
2. the file number
3. the letterhead — Ministry, Department and office
4. the place and date
5. the form’s own title, centred
6. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
7. the reference to the communication being answered — its number and its date
8. the body paragraphs
9. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
10. the addressee block
11. the list of enclosures
12. the copy-to list

Rules:
- Write in the THIRD person throughout — "the undersigned", "it is requested", never "I" or "we".
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- An urgency grading (Immediate / Priority / Top Priority — तत्काल / प्राथमिकता / परम अग्रता) may be shown at the top. Grade it only if the officer asked for one; an ungraded communication is the normal case.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.
- An interim reply says only that the matter is receiving attention and when a substantive reply may be expected. It must not anticipate the decision.

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Number and date are on the draft — Every draft put up on a file bears the file number, and the number and date of the last communication in the series must be quoted.
- Written in the third person — An Office Memorandum is written in the third person and bears no salutation or subscription.
- Signature block carries designation, telephone and email — The name, designation, telephone number, fax number and e-mail address of the signing officer must invariably be on the draft.
- The date of the final reply is named — An interim reply exists to give the party a date. Without one it says only that nothing has happened, which the party already knows.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- urgency: none
- fileNumber: A-11011/2/2026-Estt.
- ministry: Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions
- department: Department of Personnel and Training
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- addressee: The Under Secretary
Department of Expenditure
North Block, New Delhi
- subject: Interim reply — grant of Children Education Allowance for the academic year 2025-26.
- paras: The undersigned is directed to refer to the communication cited above and to say that the matter requires the comments of the Integrated Finance Division, which has been called for from the Integrated Finance Division.
A final reply will be sent by 31.07.2026.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Under Secretary to the Govt. of India
- phone: 011-2309 2590
- email: us-estt@nic.in
- reference: this Department's O.M. of even number dated 12.05.2026
- copyTo: The office order file.

Still empty: whatIsAwaited, awaitedFrom, finalReplyBy."
`;

