Structure:
1. the urgency grading, at the very top
2. the file number
3. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
4. the reference to the communication being answered — its number and its date
5. the body paragraphs
6. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
7. the footer

Rules:
- Write in the THIRD person throughout — "the undersigned", "it is requested", never "I" or "we".
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- An urgency grading (Immediate / Priority / Top Priority — तत्काल / प्राथमिकता / परम अग्रता) may be shown at the top. Grade it only if the officer asked for one; an ungraded communication is the normal case.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.
- A note on a file is written for the officer who will decide, not for the addressee of the case: state the facts, the rule, the precedent and then the precise point on which orders are sought (CSMOP 7.3).

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- Divided into serially numbered paragraphs — A note will be divided into serially numbered paragraphs; in a problem-solving or policy case the paragraphs may carry brief titles.
- Full signature with the complete date — The Dealing Officer affixes a full signature with the complete date (dd/mm/yyyy) on the left below the note; a Section Officer and above sign on the right.
- The competent authority is named — Indicate the authority competent to take the decision, along with the delegation of powers relied on.
- A course of action is proposed — Suggest the course of action to be taken with justification, along with the alternatives for the competent authority to consider.
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
