exports[`every form has an instruction > representation 1`] = `
"Form: Representation / अभ्यावेदन (id: representation).
Used by: A Government servant representing to the competent authority on a matter of personal grievance — seniority, pay fixation, transfer, a denied claim — through proper channel.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraphs 8.4(1), 8.9, Appendix 8.1.
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the place and date
2. the addressee block
3. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
4. the reference to the communication being answered — its number and its date
5. the salutation
6. the body paragraphs
7. the subscription
8. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
9. the list of enclosures

Rules:
- Write in the FIRST person — this form is one named officer writing to another.
- Open with the salutation "Sir / Madam,".
- Close with the subscription "Yours faithfully,".
- This form carries NO urgency grading.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- The order represented against is identified — The number and date of the last communication in the series must always be referred to; a representation against an unidentified order cannot be examined.
- Routed through the proper channel — A representation goes to the competent authority through the head of office, who forwards it with the Department's comments.
- The relief sought is stated — Say what you are asking for. A representation that describes a grievance without naming the relief leaves the deciding officer nothing to order.
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Paragraphs are serially numbered — The specimens leave the first paragraph unnumbered and number the rest from 2.
- Enclosures mentioned in the text are listed — A draft should clearly specify the enclosures which are to accompany the fair copy, and the number goes at the bottom left.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- addressee: The Joint Secretary (Administration)
Department of Personnel and Training
North Block, New Delhi - 110001
(Through proper channel)
- subject: Representation against fixation of pay on promotion to the post of Section Officer — regarding.
- reference: Office Order No. A-11011/4/2026-Estt. dated 12.06.2026
- paras: I respectfully submit the following representation for kind consideration against the fixation of my pay on promotion to the post of Section Officer, communicated vide the Office Order cited above.
I was promoted to the post of Section Officer with effect from 01.05.2026 and my pay was fixed at Level 8, Cell 1 of the Pay Matrix. I had exercised the option under FR 22(I)(a)(1) to have my pay fixed from the date of my next increment, which option is on record at page 11 of my service book.
The option appears not to have been given effect to. Had it been applied, my pay would have been fixed at Level 8, Cell 2 with effect from 01.07.2026, and the difference works out to Rs. 2,400 per month.
In similar circumstances, the pay of Shri A.B.C., Section Officer, was re-fixed by this Department vide Office Order No. A-11011/7/2025-Estt. dated 09.09.2025, a copy of which is enclosed.
I therefore request that my pay may kindly be re-fixed in terms of the option exercised, and the arrears released. I shall be grateful for a decision at an early date.
