exports[`every form has an instruction > rti-reply 1`] = `
"Form: Reply to an RTI application / सूचना का अधिकार आवेदन का उत्तर (id: rti-reply).
Used by: The Central Public Information Officer replying to an application under the Right to Information Act, 2005.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraphs 8.4(1), 8.9, 12.5, Appendix 8.1.
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the file number
2. the letterhead — Ministry, Department and office
3. the place and date
4. the addressee block
5. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
6. the reference to the communication being answered — its number and its date
7. the salutation
8. the body paragraphs
9. the subscription
10. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
11. the footer
12. the list of enclosures
13. the copy-to list

Rules:
- Write in the FIRST person — this form is one named officer writing to another.
- Open with the salutation "Sir / Madam,".
- Close with the subscription "Yours faithfully,".
- This form carries NO urgency grading.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.
- An RTI reply states the information, or the exemption relied on with the sub-clause of section 8(1) or 9, and it must always give the name and address of the First Appellate Authority and the thirty-day limit (RTI Act s.7, s.19(1)).

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- The First Appellate Authority is named with the 30-day limit — Section 7(8) of the Act requires the reply to state the particulars of the appellate authority and the time limit. Its absence is itself a ground of appeal.
- Answered point by point — Reply in the applicant's own numbering. A single paragraph answering four questions leaves the applicant unable to tell which was refused.
- The application date and the date of receipt are both stated — The 30 days run from receipt, not from the date the applicant wrote. Both dates on the reply are what let anyone check that it was in time.
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Signature block carries designation, telephone and email — The name, designation, telephone number, fax number and e-mail address of the signing officer must invariably be on the draft.
- Enclosures mentioned in the text are listed — A draft should clearly specify the enclosures which are to accompany the fair copy, and the number goes at the bottom left.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- fileNumber: A-11011/2/2026-Estt.
- ministry: Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions
- department: Department of Personnel and Training
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- addressee: Shri Ramesh Kumar
27, Gandhi Nagar
Meerut, Uttar Pradesh - 250002
- subject: Reply to the application dated 04.08.2026 under the Right to Information Act, 2005 — regarding.
- applicationDate: 2026-08-04
- receivedOn: 2026-08-11
- paras: Please refer to your application dated 04.08.2026 under the Right to Information Act, 2005, received in this office on 11.08.2026 and registered at No. DOPT/R/2026/60214. The information sought is furnished point-wise below.
Point 1: The number of posts of Section Officer sanctioned in this Department as on 01.04.2026 is 214, of which 187 are filled. A statement is enclosed.
Point 2: The information sought relates to the deliberations of a Departmental Promotion Committee and is exempt from disclosure under Section 8(1)(j) of the Act, being personal information the disclosure of which has no relationship to any public activity or interest.
Point 3: The information sought is not held by this Department. Your application has been transferred in respect of this point to the Central Public Information Officer, Department of Expenditure, under Section 6(3) of the Act, and you are advised accordingly.
If you are not satisfied with this reply, you may prefer a first appeal under Section 19(1) of the Act within 30 days to Shri A. K. Menon, Deputy Secretary and First Appellate Authority, Department of Personnel and Training, North Block, New Delhi - 110001.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Under Secretary and Central Public Information Officer
- phone: 011-2309 2590
