exports[`every form has an instruction > speaking-order 1`] = `
"Form: Speaking order / सकारण आदेश (id: speaking-order).
Used by: A competent authority deciding a matter that affects a person's rights.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraph 8.4(5).
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the file number
2. the letterhead — Ministry, Department and office
3. the place and date
4. the form’s own title, centred
5. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
6. the body paragraphs
7. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
8. the list of enclosures
9. the copy-to list

Rules:
- Write in the THIRD person throughout — "the undersigned", "it is requested", never "I" or "we".
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- This form carries NO urgency grading.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.
- A speaking order records the material considered, the submissions made and the reason for the conclusion, in that order — a conclusion with no reason behind it is the defect the form exists to prevent.

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Number and date are on the draft — Every draft put up on a file bears the file number, and the number and date of the last communication in the series must be quoted.
- Signature block carries designation, telephone and email — The name, designation, telephone number, fax number and e-mail address of the signing officer must invariably be on the draft.
- Reasons for the decision are recorded — An order that decides a claim without giving reasons is not a speaking order and is liable to be set aside on appeal for that reason alone.
- The appellate remedy is stated — A person told what has been decided must also be told to whom and within what time they may appeal, or the remedy is one they have to discover.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
