exports[`every form has an instruction > tour-programme 1`] = `
"Form: Tour programme / दौरा कार्यक्रम (id: tour-programme).
Used by: An officer putting up the itinerary of an official tour for the approval of the controlling authority, before the tour is undertaken.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraphs 8.4(4), Appendix 8.1.
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the urgency grading, at the very top
2. the file number
3. the letterhead — Ministry, Department and office
4. the place and date
5. the form’s own title, centred
6. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
7. the reference to the communication being answered — its number and its date
8. the body paragraphs
9. the footer
10. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
11. the list of enclosures
12. the copy-to list

Rules:
- Write in the THIRD person throughout — "the undersigned", "it is requested", never "I" or "we".
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- An urgency grading (Immediate / Priority / Top Priority — तत्काल / प्राथमिकता / परम अग्रता) may be shown at the top. Grade it only if the officer asked for one; an ungraded communication is the normal case.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- The itinerary is given date by date — The travelling allowance bill is settled against the approved itinerary; a programme without dates cannot be checked against a bill.
- The purpose of the tour is stated — The approving authority is approving an expenditure; the purpose is what it is approving it for.
- The approving authority is named — Indicate the authority competent to approve, the way a note indicates the level of disposal.
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Number and date are on the draft — Every draft put up on a file bears the file number, and the number and date of the last communication in the series must be quoted.
- Signature block carries designation, telephone and email — The name, designation, telephone number, fax number and e-mail address of the signing officer must invariably be on the draft.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- urgency: none
- fileNumber: A-11011/2/2026-Estt.
- ministry: Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions
- department: Department of Personnel and Training
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- subject: Tour programme of Shri X.Y.Z., Section Officer, from 15.09.2026 to 18.09.2026 — approval regarding.
- officerName: Shri X. Y. Zachariah
- officerDesignation: Section Officer, Level 8
- purpose: To attend the regional review meeting on implementation of e-Office version 7.0 and to inspect the Central Registration Unit of the Regional Office.
- itinerary: 15.09.2026 — Depart New Delhi 06:00 by Train 12951 (2A); arrive Mumbai 22:30. Halt at Mumbai.
16.09.2026 — Regional review meeting at the Regional Office, Mumbai, 10:00 to 17:00. Halt at Mumbai.
17.09.2026 — Inspection of the Central Registration Unit, Regional Office, Mumbai. Halt at Mumbai.
18.09.2026 — Depart Mumbai 08:00 by Train 12952 (2A); arrive New Delhi 23:35.
- paras: The tour programme of Shri X.Y.Z., Section Officer (Level 8), for the period 15.09.2026 to 18.09.2026 is placed below for approval.
Travel is proposed by rail in AC 2-tier, which is the entitlement at Level 8, and the officer will not be leaving headquarters on a public holiday. Daily allowance is claimed for three nights of halt at Mumbai.
The expenditure is debitable to the sanctioned travel budget of the Division for the current financial year, in which a balance of Rs. 3,80,000 is available.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Under Secretary to the Govt. of India
- phone: 011-2309 2590
- email: us-estt@nic.in
- approvingAuthority: Joint Secretary (Administration)
- copyTo: The officer concerned
The Drawing and Disbursing Officer
Guard file

Still empty: mainPoint."
`;

