exports[`every form has an instruction > transfer-request 1`] = `
"Form: Transfer request / स्थानांतरण अनुरोध (id: transfer-request).
Used by: An officer, on their own behalf.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraph 8.4(1).
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the place and date
2. the addressee block
3. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
4. the salutation
5. the body paragraphs
6. the subscription
7. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
8. the list of enclosures

Rules:
- Write in the FIRST person — this form is one named officer writing to another.
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- This form carries NO urgency grading.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- A ground the policy recognises is named — A request that gives no ground is decided against the general seniority position, which is rarely what the applicant wanted.
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Paragraphs are serially numbered — The specimens leave the first paragraph unnumbered and number the rest from 2.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- addressee: The Under Secretary (Establishment)
Department of Personnel and Training
North Block, New Delhi
- subject: Request for transfer to the Regional Office, Lucknow, on grounds of spouse posting.
- paras: I request that I may be considered for transfer to the Regional Office, Lucknow, on the ground that my spouse, who is also in Central Government service, has been posted at Lucknow with effect from 01.07.2026.
I have been serving at New Delhi since 15.07.2019, that is, for 7 years, and my present post is Assistant Section Officer, Establishment Section.
In support, a copy of my spouse's posting order dated 20.06.2026 is enclosed.
I shall be grateful if the request may be considered in accordance with the transfer policy of the Department. I am willing to be relieved at the convenience of the office.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Assistant Section Officer
- phone: 011-2309 2590
- email: abc@nic.in
- enclosures: A copy of my spouse's posting order dated 20.06.2026.

Still empty: requestedStation, ground, presentStation, sinceDate, durationYears, presentPost."
`;

exports[`every form has an instruction > vigilance-clearance 1`] = `
"Form: Vigilance clearance request / सतर्कता निकासी अनुरोध (id: vigilance-clearance).
Used by: An officer, on their own behalf.
CSMOP 2022, sixteenth edition, paragraph 8.4(3).
CSMOP prescribes no format for this document. This form follows the format of the nearest prescribed one; say nothing that claims the Manual specifies it.

Structure:
1. the place and date
2. the addressee block
3. the subject line, one sentence, ending in “regarding.” or “के संबंध में।”
4. the salutation
5. the body paragraphs
6. the subscription
7. the signature block — name, designation, telephone and e-mail
8. the list of enclosures

Rules:
- Write in the FIRST person — this form is one named officer writing to another.
- This form carries NO salutation.
- This form carries NO subscription.
- This form carries NO urgency grading.
- Hindi register: use the administrative Hindi of the Central Secretariat (Rajbhasha) — "कार्यालय ज्ञापन", "अवर सचिव", "एतद्द्वारा" — and not everyday or literary Hindi. Keep file numbers, section numbers and English proper names in their original form.
- Leave anything you were not told as four underscores (____). Never invent a file number, a date, an amount, a name or a designation.

The document will be marked against this checklist, by the app, after you answer. Every item below must pass:
- Both disciplinary and vigilance status are asked about — Clearance on disciplinary proceedings is not clearance on a vigilance case; a request that asks about one gets an answer about one.
- The subject is stated — The specimens in Appendix 8.1 carry a subject line above the body on every form that is addressed to anyone.
- Paragraphs are serially numbered — The specimens leave the first paragraph unnumbered and number the rest from 2.
- No placeholder is left unfilled — A draft that goes out with {{…}} still in it has not been read.

What the officer has already written. Complete it — do not replace what is there:
- place: New Delhi
- date: 2026-08-28
- addressee: The Vigilance Officer
Department of Personnel and Training
North Block, New Delhi
- subject: Vigilance clearance in respect of Shri A.B.C., Section Officer, for deputation.
- paras: Vigilance clearance is requested in respect of Shri A.B.C., Section Officer, for deputation to the Department of Expenditure, covering the period the last ten years.
It may kindly be confirmed whether any disciplinary proceedings under the CCS (CCA) Rules, 1965 are pending or contemplated against the officer, and whether any vigilance case, complaint or investigation is pending.
The information is required by 20.09.2026, as the proposal has to be submitted to the Department of Expenditure by that date.
- signatoryName: A.B.C.
- signatoryDesignation: Under Secretary to the Govt. of India
- phone: 011-2309 2590
- email: abc@nic.in
- enclosures: The deputation proposal in respect of the officer.

Still empty: officerName, officerDesignation, purpose, period, replyBy, submitTo."
